    Remove typesafe config from the db module (#8227)
    
    The db bundle embedded the typesafe config library only because
    mchange-commons, which c3p0 is built on, can read HOCON configuration
    files if the library is available. Opencast does not use that. It
    configures the connection pool programmatically, and the bundle contains
    no HOCON files which c3p0 could read.
    
    Without the library, c3p0 skips the HOCON configuration with a debug
    message and still reads its configuration from properties files and
    system properties. The package is excluded from the bundle imports, so
    these stay unchanged.
    
    Dropping it shrinks the bundle by about 290 KB.
    
    This is part of #8214.
    
